phasizes the need to balance model complexity and generalizability.\n\nIn practice, estimation error can be assessed using various diagnostic tools, such as residual analysis, which examines the differences between observed and predicted values. A well-specified model should exhibit residuals that are randomly distributed around zero, indicating that the estimation error is minimized. Conversely, patterns in the residuals may signal model misspecification or the presence of omitted variable bias, leading to increased estimation error.\n\nIn summary, estimation error is a critical concept in regression analysis that quantifies the difference between estimated and true values of coefficients. It serves as a key indicator of model accuracy and reliability, influencing the validity of statistical inferences. By understanding the sources and implications of estimation error, econometricians can enhance model performance and ensure that their analyses yield meaningful insights.", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": [], "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null}, "content_filter_results": {"hate": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "protected_material_code": {"filtered": false, "detected": false}, "protected_material_text": {"filtered": false, "detected": false}, "self_harm": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "sexual": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "violence": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}}}], "created": 1771166092, "model": "gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": "fp_f97eff32c5", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 478, "prompt_tokens": 308, "total_tokens": 786, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "rejected_prediction_tokens": 0}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 0}}, "prompt_filter_results": [{"prompt_index": 0, "content_filter_results": {"hate": {"filtered